{"type":"message","id":"510e65a3","parentId":"d4c4f965","timestamp":"2026-05-24T19:15:24.561Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only automated heartbeat messages, no human discussions. The latest messages are from 23:50 UTC (timestamps around 17789755xxxx). Current time is 19:15 UTC on May 24th, 2026.\n\nWait - the heartbeat messages show timestamps like 1778975520833 which convert to roughly 23:50 UTC. But the cron says current time is Sunday, May 24th, 2026 - 7:15 PM (UTC) = 19:15 UTC.\n\nThe heartbeat messages in the thread appear to be from a different time (23:xx UTC which would be 11:xx PM). But the cron task time is 19:15 UTC.\n\nLet me calculate: 1778975520833 ms timestamp → that's Unix timestamp around 1778975520 seconds. Let me check: Unix timestamp for 2026-05-24 23:50 UTC would be around 1778975400 (rough calc: 2026 is about 56 years after 1970, ~1767244800 for 2026-01-01, plus ~5749200 for May 24). Actually 1778975520 / 60 / 60 / 24 = 1778975520 / 86400 ≈ 20589 days from 1970. That's around 2026.\n\nThe timestamps seem to be around 23:50 UTC based on the content, but the cron says it's 19:15 UTC. This is a 4+ hour gap.\n\nActually, looking at the content - the messages show times like 23:50 UTC, and they're from \"another heartbeat system\". The cron task is running at 19:15 UTC. There are no human messages in either thread.\n\nI should report the heartbeat status and confirm no human discussions need response. Let me post a heartbeat to both threads.\n","thinkingSignature":"99bb4d50021fcaa162153c28924cfc57785ddaaec7968ae22e2e1dabc140b8eb"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n两线程均只有自动心跳消息，无人类讨论。最新消息时间约23:50 UTC，当前cron执行时间19:15 UTC，存在约4.5小时时间差。\n\n两线程均无新增人类讨论，无需回应。发送本次心跳：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ypwb5hcoh39s_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: appli